/-!
# Shared packed row data

The marked ATLAS matrices have 2808 distinct rows among their 5616 images.
This file records those rows and the two proposed successor indices. The proofs
in `RowChecks` verify the packed multiplication, without any field-arithmetic
assumption. Values outside the table have a harmless default.

Numerical source: Wilson, Nickerson and Bray, ATLAS L33G1-f16r16aB0;
see `SixteenModels.Data` for attribution and the coefficient convention.
The generator under `Table/source` only proposes data; Lean checks every edge.
-/

